# Deny everything, then re-admit what the demo image needs.
#
# This direction is deliberate. An allowlist that starts from "nothing" cannot
# leak a directory someone adds later; a denylist can, and the thing it would
# leak here is 665 MB of real Gujarat CCTV imagery with camera site names burned
# into the pixels. The Dockerfile's COPY lines are the actual selection -- this
# file makes a mistake in them fail rather than quietly ship.
*

# --- application source ----------------------------------------------------
!app/
app/devui/
# The developer console is unreachable in production (require_developer_ui
# returns 404), but there is no reason for its source to be in the image.

!scripts/__init__.py
!requirements-demo.txt

# --- the synthetic dataset, and only the synthetic dataset -----------------
!data/demo/

# Everything below is excluded by the `*` above and listed only so the reasons
# are on the record, not because the rule needs restating:
#
#   .env                  government portal credentials (CCTV_ACCESS_TOKEN)
#   data/cctv.db          32 real RTSP endpoints, 5,279 real observations
#   data/evidence/        24,071 real crops, bystanders, burned-in site names
#   data/samples/         28 MB of raw government CCTV video
#   data/frames/          includes 7 real live-preview grabs
#   data/runs/            788 real evaluation crops
#   data/models/          OpenVINO weights; the demo runs no inference
#   final_report/         screenshots and demo video embed real imagery
#   yolov8n.pt            AGPL-3.0 weights; nothing in the demo detects anything
#   .git/                 full history
